# Issue #1364: files that are deliberately not valid cnx.
#
# Two shapes. Most are fixtures asserting their own *syntax* error, with a
# committed .expected.error beside them to prove it. One is a HELPER that carries
# the error its sibling asserts: a cross-file diagnostic has to put the offending
# construct in the included file, so nested-lib.cnx is unparseable on purpose and
# cross-file-nested.expected.error is where the assertion lives (#1306).
#
# A formatter cannot format what it cannot parse, and Prettier treats an
# unparseable file as an error rather than skipping it, so these are excluded by
# name. This is a registry, not a mute button: `npm run format:fidelity` fails
# BOTH ways -- on a file the parser rejects that is missing here, and on a file
# listed here that parses fine -- so nothing can be silenced by adding it.
